h a message instead of a traceback.\n- **Sort order:** Rows are sorted by the whole `name` text, ignoring upper/lower case. So \"Grace Hopper\" sorts under G, not under Hopper. If you want the phone list ordered by surname, say so and I'll change it.\n- **Equal names:** Rows with the same name keep their original order.\n- **Columns and quoting:** The header and all columns are written back in their original order, and quoted fields such as `\"Smith, Zed\"` stay intact.\n- **Line endings:** The output uses Windows-style `\\r\\n` line endings, which is the default of Python's `csv` module. Spreadsheets and printing handle them fine.\n- **Byte-order mark:** A BOM at the start of the input, which Excel often adds, is accepted and dropped from the output.\n\nThe code is in `contacts/cli.py`, and the tests are in `tests/test_cli.py`. To run the tests, use `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`.","ttft_ms":4103,"type":"result","duration_ms":29132,"uuid":"0ad59f12-c815-4a44-8d2c-9e3930a23fad","ttft_stream_ms":1040,"time_to_request_ms":97,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":24,"system_prompt":17,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":1,"tool_pool_refresh":3,"init_message":3,"engine_pickup":1,"autocompact":2,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":14,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":10,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":47,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":117,"time_to_request_major_faults":73,"first_content_frame_ms":1040,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
